--- freertos/FreeRTOS.h & freertos/task.h ---
allows esp32 to do multiple task at a time: read sensor, send wifi, all at once
Important commands: vTaskDelay(miliseconds)
documentation: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32/api-reference/system/freertos.html


--- esp_system.h / esp_log.h ---
esp_system gives the user chip-level utilities like restarting, reseting...
Important commands: 
    esp_restart()
    esp_reset_reason() -- tells why chip booted
    esp_get_free_heap_size() / esp_get_minimum_free_heap_size -- check memory
    esp_register_shutdown_handler() -- run cleanup code before a restart
    esp_random() -- generate random number
Documentation: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32/migration-guides/release-5.x/5.0/system.html

esp_log is like printing out commands. Instead of normal printf, one can define a severity level and source name
 - > one can filter messages by level. 
 - > Filter by tag at runtime: example : esp_log_level_set("wifi", ESP_LOG_WARN)
Important commands:
    static const char *TAG = "name";  - > set the name of the tag
    ESP_LOGE(TAG, "big error: %d", err); - > prints RED error
    ESP_LOGW(TAG, "warning);  - > prints YELLOW warning
    ESP_LOGI(TAG, "information");  - > prints GREEN general information
    ESP_LOGD(TAG, "x = %d, x)  - > detailed infomation debug [hidden by default] 
    ESP_LOGV(TAG, "detailed trace") - > detailed verbose tracing of code [hidden by default]
Documentation: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32/api-reference/system/log.html


--- onewire_bus.h ---
This library provdes an medium for communicating with Dallas/Maxim 1-Wire devices: ds18b20 thermometer
 - > supports RMT and UART backends
 - > handles low-level timing requirements of 1-Wire protocol 
Important commands: 
    onewire_bus_config_t bus_config = {   - > configuration
      .bus_gpio_num = **GPIO pin number**
      .flags = { 
        .en_pull_up = false/true  - > status of the internal pull-up resistor of the esp32
      }
    }
    onewire_bus_rmt_config_t rmt_config = {    - > RMT backend configuration
      .max_rx_bytes = 10,      - > maximum bytes expected in a single receive operation
    }
    onewire_bus_handle_t bus = NULL   - > create 1-wirebus handle
    plenty more: check documentation
Documentation: https://espressif.github.io/idf-extra-components/latest/onewire_bus/index.html


